ption><table frame="hsides" rules="groups"><thead><tr><th valign="top" align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Objectives of the health care system</th><th valign="top" align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Individual clinical practice level</th><th valign="top" align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Intervention program level</th><th valign="top" align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Systemic level</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td valign="top" align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1"><bold>Effectiveness</bold></td><td valign="top" align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Beneficial effects of individual clinical interventions on the state of individuals' health</td><td valign="top" align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Beneficial effects of clinical interventions organized and developed by multidisciplinary clinical teams coordinating around the health of individuals</td><td valign="top" align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Beneficial effects of integrated modes of health service regulation, production and management on populations' health</td></tr><tr><td valign="top" align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1"><bold>Efficiency</bold></td><td valign="top" align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Maximization of the beneficial effects of individual clinical interventions on utilization and distribution of limited resources</td><td valign="top" align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Maximization of the beneficial health effects of coordinated multi-disciplinary clinical interventions on utilization and distribution of limited resources</td><td valign="top" align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">In a context of limited resources, maximization of the beneficial effects of integrated modes of service regulation, production and management on populations' health</td></tr><tr><td valign="top" align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1"><bold>Equity</bold></td><td valign="top" align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Beneficial effects of individual clinical interventions on health disparities</td><td valign="top" align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Beneficial effects of coordinated multidisciplinary clinical interventions on health disparities</td><td valign="top" align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Beneficial effects of integrated modes of service regulation, production, and management of health disparities between populations</td></tr></tbody></table></table-wrap><table-wrap id="tb002" position="float"><label>Table 2</label><caption><p>Definitions of integration by objectives/levels of the healthcare system</p></caption><table frame="hsides" rules="groups"><thead><tr><th valign="top" align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Objectives of the health care system</th><th valign="top" align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Individual clinical practice level</th><th valign="top" align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Intervention program level</th><th valign="top" align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Systemic level</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td valign="top" align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">&#x02002;Effectiveness</td><td valign="top" align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">&#x02022;&#x02003;Continuity of care</td><td valign="top" align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">&#x02022;&#x02003;Collective coordination</td><td valign="top" align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">&#x02022;&#x02003;Collaboration</td></tr><tr><td valign="top" align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">&#x02002;Efficiency</td><td valign="top" align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">&#x02022;&#x02003;Sequential coordination</td><td valign="top" align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">&#x02022;&#x02003;Professional integration</td><td valign="top" align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">&#x02022;&#x02003;Functional integration</td></tr><tr><td valign="top" align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">&#x02002;Equity</td><td valign="top" align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">&#x02022;&#x02003;Reciprocal coordination</td><td valign="top" align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">&#x02022;&#x02003;Clinical integration</td><td valign="top" align="left